WEBVTT

00:00:09.400 --> 00:00:11.210
Twenty Faces?

00:00:11.210 --> 00:00:14.450
Yeah.  Apparently he has twenty different faces.

00:00:14.450 --> 00:00:17.030
If that was true, he'd be some kind of monster.

00:00:17.030 --> 00:00:19.550
No, that's not what I meant.

00:00:25.480 --> 00:00:29.830
Would you like one?  They're cold and sweet.

00:00:30.900 --> 00:00:32.290
We'll take two.

00:00:32.290 --> 00:00:33.870
Thank you very much.

00:00:36.170 --> 00:00:36.930
Here.

00:00:42.920 --> 00:00:46.810
What I meant was he makes use of many different faces.

00:00:46.810 --> 00:00:47.930
Disguises then?

00:00:47.930 --> 00:00:52.940
Yeah.  And he's... coming here... to steal...

00:00:53.460 --> 00:00:54.970
Sh-She couldn't have...

00:01:05.360 --> 00:01:09.840
I'm one of his twenty faces too.

00:02:38.830 --> 00:02:43.620
This year marks the 300th anniversary of the building of our town, Toran.

00:02:43.620 --> 00:02:51.390
In celebration of this year, it brings me great pride as your mayor to gather the townspeople together for this magnificent festival.

00:02:51.390 --> 00:02:58.870
In particular, the town is showing in our museum an exceedingly valuable treasure of world-class historical merit.

00:02:58.870 --> 00:03:03.290
The Clock of the Three Magi, now on special public display.

00:03:04.180 --> 00:03:11.490
Also, we've invited the very famous circus troupe, the Orion Troupe, all the way from America.

00:03:33.730 --> 00:03:37.440
We're supposed to be clowns, so we need to make them laugh more, Muta.

00:03:37.440 --> 00:03:41.770
And you need to look a little sexier, Hans.

00:03:41.770 --> 00:03:44.990
You're my knife-throwing target, after all.

00:03:44.990 --> 00:03:48.410
You need to yell out "Ahh!" in a really sexy voice, OK?

00:03:48.410 --> 00:03:50.970
Why do I have to dress up as a fräulein?

00:03:50.970 --> 00:03:54.780
The audience isn't going to enjoy seeing me throw knives at a man.

00:03:54.780 --> 00:03:55.790
Right, Chiko?

00:03:57.290 --> 00:04:00.210
Man, she's not listening to me.

00:04:02.690 --> 00:04:05.800
Oh, they mentioned our job in there.

00:04:05.800 --> 00:04:08.060
Chiko's really into it.

00:04:08.060 --> 00:04:09.680
What I'm reading is this here.

00:04:11.100 --> 00:04:12.070
What is it?

00:04:12.070 --> 00:04:15.760
The Orion Troupe gained great popularity in America last year.

00:04:15.760 --> 00:04:19.680
Their most famous member is the magician of the century, Baron Doyle.

00:04:19.680 --> 00:04:27.820
His exotic appearance is, of course, very popular with the ladies and his disappearing act is to a level of opulence that has never been seen before.

00:04:27.820 --> 00:04:32.200
Also, the troupe's star performer Lily's tightrope walking act is a sight to behold.

00:04:32.200 --> 00:04:37.700
Though she just looks like a beautiful young lady, she displays a courage that's rare even among adults.

00:04:37.700 --> 00:04:40.730
One would never guess that she's a child of very few years.

00:04:41.280 --> 00:04:42.770
A child, eh?

00:04:42.770 --> 00:04:43.740
Well, excuse me.

00:04:43.740 --> 00:04:47.090
Chiko, did they say anything about my knife-throwing?

00:04:47.660 --> 00:04:48.530
Nope.

00:04:48.530 --> 00:04:48.970
Heh.

00:04:50.350 --> 00:04:52.820
Calling me a child...

00:04:52.820 --> 00:04:54.850
I'm almost thirteen!

00:04:55.750 --> 00:04:59.640
L-L-Ladies and gentlemen.

00:04:59.640 --> 00:05:07.550
A-Appearing next is our own Orion Troupe's star performer, Lily!

00:05:31.730 --> 00:05:33.620
Man, Chiko's pretty good.

00:05:51.520 --> 00:05:54.140
She scared me for a second there, but I guess it's part of the act.

00:06:08.100 --> 00:06:09.300
What's wrong, Chiko?

00:06:09.300 --> 00:06:12.310
Go wave at the audience or something.

00:06:13.760 --> 00:06:16.000
I was so scared!

00:06:16.000 --> 00:06:20.310
I thought I was going to fall.  I lost my footing after that flip.

00:06:20.310 --> 00:06:24.070
Don't be an idiot.  You shouldn't push your luck so much.

00:06:24.070 --> 00:06:25.260
Yeah, yeah.

00:06:27.910 --> 00:06:30.310
Well, looks like it's my turn.

00:06:30.310 --> 00:06:31.690
Shall I kick it up a notch?

00:06:32.790 --> 00:06:34.720
Is that because of Chiko's influence?

00:06:37.750 --> 00:06:40.950
Just don't mess up my introduction.

00:06:47.750 --> 00:06:50.180
Now, what you've all been waiting for.

00:06:50.180 --> 00:06:53.610
The dazzling magic stylings of Baron Doyle.

00:06:53.610 --> 00:06:55.180
Enjoy the show!

00:07:49.890 --> 00:07:51.040
It's pretty, isn't it?

00:07:54.400 --> 00:07:57.380
The east window is blue.  The south is red.

00:07:57.380 --> 00:08:00.150
The west is made up of purple stained glass.

00:08:00.150 --> 00:08:04.710
That way the clock changes color depending on the position of the sun.

00:08:05.760 --> 00:08:07.220
You were here yesterday too, weren't you?

00:08:08.210 --> 00:08:13.060
Hey, you're that girl from the Orion Troupe!  Their star performer, Lily!

00:08:15.090 --> 00:08:18.260
I really enjoyed the performance!

00:08:18.260 --> 00:08:21.370
Your tightrope act was great too, of course!

00:08:21.370 --> 00:08:24.570
Hey, let's be friends!

00:08:24.570 --> 00:08:26.230
I'm not going to be here very long.

00:08:26.230 --> 00:08:30.730
Wow, you're traveling the world!  That's so incredible!

00:08:32.940 --> 00:08:34.490
My name's Angie.

00:08:34.490 --> 00:08:36.580
I live here with my father.

00:08:36.580 --> 00:08:37.870
In the museum?

00:08:37.870 --> 00:08:41.240
Yeah.  My father's in charge of security.

00:08:41.240 --> 00:08:44.010
Isn't my house pretty neat?

00:08:44.010 --> 00:08:46.750
It's like they're all my own personal treasures.

00:08:49.130 --> 00:08:52.260
How about you, Lily?  Is yours a circus family?

00:08:52.260 --> 00:08:57.470
Yeah.  I guess my family are all in the circus.

00:08:57.470 --> 00:08:59.610
I'm so jealous!

00:08:59.610 --> 00:09:01.770
I've always loved the circus.

00:09:05.730 --> 00:09:07.270
Stop by tomorrow too, will you?

00:09:07.270 --> 00:09:10.720
Ah, you won't have to pay another admission fee.

00:09:10.720 --> 00:09:11.980
I'll get you in secretly.

00:09:13.490 --> 00:09:17.490
In exchange, next time teach me how you do that flip, OK?

00:09:22.790 --> 00:09:25.290
See you again tomorrow, Lily!

00:09:44.980 --> 00:09:48.980
The Orion Troupe's performance was a big success it seems.

00:09:50.110 --> 00:09:52.110
So, about what we discussed earlier...

00:09:52.960 --> 00:09:55.690
I've made the preparations that you wanted.

00:09:58.210 --> 00:10:02.080
Dinner's ready!  It's dinner time!

00:10:03.390 --> 00:10:05.390
Whew, I'm starving!

00:10:11.380 --> 00:10:12.410
Delicious!

00:10:12.410 --> 00:10:13.660
Hey, that was mine.

00:10:13.660 --> 00:10:15.520
Oh, come on.  Don't tell me you're hungry.

00:10:15.520 --> 00:10:16.650
Of course I'm starving!

00:10:16.650 --> 00:10:18.550
You already finished, Muta-nii?

00:10:21.300 --> 00:10:23.680
There's plenty for seconds.

00:10:23.680 --> 00:10:25.080
OK!

00:10:25.080 --> 00:10:26.060
I'll have seconds.

00:10:26.060 --> 00:10:28.560
Me too, Chiko.

00:10:28.560 --> 00:10:31.520
Mister, I'll dish you up some stew.

00:10:31.520 --> 00:10:33.570
Ah, yes please.

00:10:37.860 --> 00:10:39.440
You're in good spirits today.

00:10:39.440 --> 00:10:40.710
Did something happen?

00:10:41.410 --> 00:10:45.880
I made friends with a girl at the museum.

00:10:45.880 --> 00:10:48.700
So you've been going there everyday like I asked.

00:10:48.700 --> 00:10:49.720
Yes.

00:10:49.720 --> 00:10:50.730
Thank you.

00:10:51.680 --> 00:10:54.200
Can you make a rough sketch of the interior?

00:10:54.200 --> 00:10:56.180
I drew one up yesterday.

00:10:56.180 --> 00:10:57.120
Oh?

00:11:00.100 --> 00:11:01.340
That looks pretty accurate.

00:11:01.340 --> 00:11:06.410
Here on the second floor is where the guards stay.  The basement is the storeroom.

00:11:06.410 --> 00:11:08.850
I didn't ask you to do anything, so why did you draw this sketch?

00:11:08.850 --> 00:11:12.800
I figured there must be a reason why I've been going to the museum.

00:11:12.800 --> 00:11:16.730
Oh, you've picked up the essentials of our job pretty thoroughly.

00:11:16.730 --> 00:11:20.970
Well, we have been together for two years now.

00:11:20.970 --> 00:11:23.700
And you've improved your agility quite a bit too.

00:11:24.770 --> 00:11:26.950
I guess we can't call you a kid anymore.

00:11:33.080 --> 00:11:35.960
And you even discovered the rooms where the on-site guards live.

00:11:37.360 --> 00:11:38.460
Well, about that...

00:11:39.620 --> 00:11:42.470
Is it the girl you made friends with today?

00:12:01.950 --> 00:12:03.110
Angie?

00:12:04.390 --> 00:12:06.940
Lily!  I've been waiting for you.

00:12:08.430 --> 00:12:09.540
Angie.

00:12:14.000 --> 00:12:16.490
I'm so glad you came again today.

00:12:17.170 --> 00:12:18.370
Follow me.

00:12:27.550 --> 00:12:29.340
We'll sneak in through the back.

00:12:48.900 --> 00:12:51.060
See?  Wasn't that easy?

00:12:52.380 --> 00:12:53.760
Yeah.

00:12:53.760 --> 00:12:57.360
A thief could sneak in through there really easily.

00:12:58.850 --> 00:13:00.440
I guess so.

00:13:00.440 --> 00:13:04.120
But my dad would lose his job if that actually happened.

00:13:04.120 --> 00:13:06.070
I'd be in trouble too.

00:13:08.340 --> 00:13:11.050
Listen, I need to get going.

00:13:11.050 --> 00:13:15.370
No!  You haven't showed me how you do your flips yet!

00:13:15.370 --> 00:13:17.210
Also, look.

00:13:18.840 --> 00:13:23.030
Watch.  Out of nowhere, it moved to the other hand!

00:13:24.570 --> 00:13:29.080
Oh no!  I've got to pick them all up or I'll get yelled at!

00:13:34.040 --> 00:13:37.560
Wow, you're mean.  You just laughed, didn't you?

00:13:37.560 --> 00:13:39.260
I'm sorry.

00:13:39.260 --> 00:13:41.700
I've practiced this too.

00:13:41.700 --> 00:13:42.420
See.

00:13:42.420 --> 00:13:44.700
Wow!

00:13:44.700 --> 00:13:49.340
Our hands aren't as big as an adult's.  You can't try to hold onto too many at once.

00:13:49.340 --> 00:13:52.760
Wow, you can even do sleight of hand.

00:13:54.700 --> 00:13:57.450
I guess I'll never be able to join the circus.

00:13:57.450 --> 00:13:59.770
You wanted to join the circus?

00:13:59.770 --> 00:14:00.940
Yeah, but I gave that up.

00:14:01.790 --> 00:14:04.560
I'm not cut out for it.  I'm too clumsy.

00:14:05.340 --> 00:14:07.950
Right.  Maybe that's a good thing.

00:14:09.160 --> 00:14:11.410
What did you say?!

00:14:19.220 --> 00:14:21.710
See you again, Lily!

00:14:22.230 --> 00:14:24.210
I'll be waiting here again tomorrow.

00:14:25.230 --> 00:14:26.210
OK.

00:14:48.320 --> 00:14:49.910
Damn him, sneaking in there.

00:14:56.700 --> 00:14:58.800
You want something from me?

00:14:58.800 --> 00:15:00.240
Who are you working for?

00:15:00.240 --> 00:15:00.850
Tiger.

00:15:11.480 --> 00:15:14.770
That's a greeting from me to Twenty Faces.

00:15:28.210 --> 00:15:30.150
See ya, boy.

00:15:46.510 --> 00:15:49.500
Do you want to sit out the job this time?

00:15:50.170 --> 00:15:52.190
Mister, I...

00:15:52.190 --> 00:15:52.880
Boss!

00:15:52.880 --> 00:15:54.930
W-We've got trouble!

00:15:54.930 --> 00:15:56.930
Ken!  It's Ken!

00:16:00.950 --> 00:16:02.320
Ken-niichan!

00:16:03.400 --> 00:16:07.170
The medicine finally kicked in and calmed him down.

00:16:07.170 --> 00:16:08.790
Was it Tiger?

00:16:08.790 --> 00:16:10.190
He's still alive?

00:16:10.190 --> 00:16:12.760
Is it you he's after, or the treasure?

00:16:12.760 --> 00:16:15.030
We can do it better than him.

00:16:15.600 --> 00:16:16.890
Ken-niichan!

00:16:16.890 --> 00:16:20.080
He came to challenge you, Boss.

00:16:20.080 --> 00:16:25.360
But it won't be so simple with Tiger in the picture now.

00:16:25.360 --> 00:16:27.610
And with you injured like this...

00:16:27.610 --> 00:16:28.840
I'm going too!

00:16:28.840 --> 00:16:29.610
Ken.

00:16:30.700 --> 00:16:32.840
Don't overexert yourself.

00:16:33.510 --> 00:16:36.840
I'll make up for my own mistakes.

00:16:38.630 --> 00:16:40.480
Just rest, Ken-niichan.

00:16:40.480 --> 00:16:41.100
Chiko.

00:16:42.230 --> 00:16:44.170
I'll do it.

00:16:44.170 --> 00:16:48.970
Times like this are why you and everyone else taught me all those things!

00:16:57.080 --> 00:17:00.370
Hey, if you have any apprehensions, you'd better stop now.

00:17:03.020 --> 00:17:05.250
Thank you.  I appreciate your concern.

00:17:07.250 --> 00:17:09.180
I'll go prepare dinner.

00:17:16.070 --> 00:17:17.910
Hey, what's this about?

00:17:17.910 --> 00:17:20.160
It's a real feast tonight.

00:17:20.160 --> 00:17:22.210
Tonight's our last performance.

00:17:22.210 --> 00:17:26.640
Yeah, we need our strength for the job we're about to do.

00:17:26.640 --> 00:17:28.810
Make sure to eat some vegetables too, Yasu-san.

00:17:28.810 --> 00:17:30.410
Yes, ma'am.

00:17:30.410 --> 00:17:31.520
Hey, Chiko.

00:17:31.520 --> 00:17:36.030
Hans is getting fan letters from men.  All of these.

00:17:36.030 --> 00:17:38.540
That's incredible, Hans-san!

00:17:38.540 --> 00:17:42.050
Maybe I'll try and become the new star of the circus.

00:17:42.050 --> 00:17:45.310
Chiko, let's do the trapeze together next time.

00:17:45.310 --> 00:17:45.910
OK!

00:17:45.910 --> 00:17:48.670
Part of me wants to see that and part of me doesn't.

00:17:50.180 --> 00:17:51.150
My sentiments exactly.

00:17:59.340 --> 00:18:02.270
Ladies and gentlemen.

00:18:02.270 --> 00:18:07.050
Tonight is the Orion Troupe's final performance in this town.

00:18:07.050 --> 00:18:10.530
Please cheer us on as much as you can.

00:18:33.970 --> 00:18:35.710
OK, hurry and go.

00:19:09.130 --> 00:19:11.790
You did good, finding this way in.

00:19:16.150 --> 00:19:17.090
I'm going in.

00:20:15.970 --> 00:20:18.840
Ladies and gentlemen, I'm afraid it's time to say farewell.

00:20:20.010 --> 00:20:22.160
Thank you all very much.

00:20:31.810 --> 00:20:32.460
What's that?!

00:20:32.460 --> 00:20:33.340
What is that?

00:20:33.340 --> 00:20:34.150
Isn't that an airship?

00:20:34.850 --> 00:20:35.370
What's it doing there?

00:20:48.930 --> 00:20:50.970
You did good, Chiko.
